# Controls what `git archive` exports. It does not affect `git clone`, `git
# log`, GitHub, or anything else about this repo's history — everything
# marked `export-ignore` stays exactly as tracked, everywhere else.
#
# This repo is the working one: full history, the whole _AI_CONTEXT/ pack,
# every handoff note. A second, client-facing repo is what actually deploys,
# connected to the VPS through its Docker manager, and it has no business
# carrying the internal planning trail. `scripts/export-client-repo.sh`
# builds that second repo's tree with `git archive`, which silently drops
# everything listed below.
#
# Add a path here the day it becomes "ours, not the client's" — a new session
# handoff file, a new folder under _BUILD. Nothing enforces that the list
# stays current; it is read, not generated.

# The AI context pack: every file whose job is telling a future Claude
# session what this project is and where things are.
_AI_CONTEXT/         export-ignore
CLAUDE.md            export-ignore

# Planning and session state. Useful to us mid-project, meaningless once the
# thing is built and running on the client's own infrastructure.
handoff/             export-ignore
_BUILD/              export-ignore
EXECUTION_PLAN.md    export-ignore
PRODUCT.md           export-ignore

# Third-party tooling notices, not project documentation.
AGENTS.md            export-ignore

# Describes the AI context pack itself ("drop these into the repo root"),
# not the application. A client repo wants a real README or none; this one
# would be actively misleading sitting at its root.
README.md            export-ignore

# docs/ is deliberately NOT listed. DEPLOYMENT.md, REPO_MAP.md and
# TYPOGRAPHY.md are engineering reference for whoever runs this in
# production, which is exactly the client repo's audience.

# Shell scripts always LF, regardless of core.autocrlf. This repo is
# developed on Windows; a script checked out with CRLF line endings breaks
# the moment git-bash tries to run it — the shebang line and every `read`
# prompt in scripts/export-client-repo.sh included.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/backup.sh text eol=lf
